{# lede #}<span class="text-white">Enterprise Jamstack Wiki Platform</span>&nbsp; for <b>creating, managing, and delivering</b> static webpages using Jamstack Technology for dynamic features therein{# lede #}. For pricing information, see our [Orion Plans](plans).

&nbsp;

### Here's the ROI, Executive Decision Maker :fa-chart-line:...

<span class="text-white">Why Choose Orion? The Jamstack Wiki Platform That Outperforms &mdash; and Costs Far Less</span>

&nbsp;

What truly sets Orion apart isn't just another wiki platform &mdash; it's our proprietary Orion Technology, a battle-tested, patent-pending approach that delivers an elegant user experience with unmatched security, reliability and efficiency.

&nbsp;

This lets us run ultra-low operating costs while offering superior editorial controls, enterprise-grade security, and groundbreaking features no legacy wiki can match. We pass those massive savings directly to you. Expect only modest, transparent upcharges for the exact cloud resources you use &mdash; no bloated pricing tiers or hidden fees.

&nbsp;

Nothing will yield better ROI than Orion in the Knowledge Management System space.  We tailor every installation to your specific requirements, and are always available for consultation and professional coaching to ensure you maximize returns on your investment in our products and services.

&nbsp;

Your **team has a partner in us** in terms of ensuring you see the productivity gains associated with Orion &mdash; designed for robust, verified, collaborative knowledge creation; and easy, comprehensive, precision information retrieval thereof.

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Leave the financially draining pain points of the past behind...</span>

For a lot of firms, Jira is a wonderfully effective tool for project management. However, over time you begin to realize that [Confluence is just tagging along for the ride](https://projectmanagers.net/top-10-cons-disadvantages-of-using-confluence/)...

If that resonates, are you tired of throwing more good money at a bad investment because of the disjointed, denormalized, unmaintainable, stale, link-rotted Confluence mess with a lousy Text Editor and even lousier Search Engine?

&nbsp;

Don't want to instead waste precious capital on an expensive, bloated, unreliable, one-size-fits-all OCD-lover's platform that cannot fulfill its enhanced productivity promises, like Notion?

&nbsp;

Want a more conservative approach than simply exposing all of your corporate secrets to unscrupulous AI vendors and their ill-gotten frontier models?

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Orion is built for leaders who refuse to settle:</span>

<div class="fade">

- :fa-school-flag: **University leaders** &mdash; Eliminate campus plagiarism and empower secure, open-access collaboration with version-controlled document sharing, curation, and online publishing. Transform your academic knowledge management into a modern, auditable, [Open Science](https://www.iconoclasts.blog/joe/triple-products) platform.

</div>

&nbsp;

<div class="fade">
<center>
<img src="index.page/hipaa" style="width:25%">
</center>

- :fa-building-columns: **Health Care, Government &amp; defense IT decision-makers** &mdash; Meet FedRAMP infrastructure, NIST 800-207 zero-trust and HIPAA requirements. Enjoy fine-grained access controls on your version-control repository &mdash; all with FIPS 140-3 compliant security and installable inside your VPN.

</div>

&nbsp;

<div class="fade">

- :fa-cart-arrow-down: **Marketing executives** &mdash; Run a fast, global, innovative enterprise platform for corporate website assets. Use Orion as a powerful headless CMS &mdash; secure, performant, and fully decoupled from frontend delivery.

</div>

&nbsp;

<div class="fade">

- :fa-computer: **Technology companies &amp; website agencies** &mdash; Replace insecure commercial wikis, tame mountains of product documentation, client sites, and even binary downloads. Curate everything with confidence, speed, and ironclad version history.

</div>

&nbsp;

<div class="fade">

- :fa-compass-drafting: **High-availability architects &amp; principled engineers** &mdash; Escape the single points of failure baked into SQL-based LAMP stacks. Embrace true Jamstack scalability: concurrent builds, incremental updates, global POP coverage, and peak performance measured in milliseconds.

</div>

&nbsp;

<div class="fade">

- :fa-business-time: **Any business tired of wiki economics** &mdash; Ditch expensive SaaS subscriptions, fragile free tools that drain staff time, and outdated systems that slow your team down. Orion gives you enterprise power at a fraction of the total cost of ownership (often under $25,000/year for full enterprise use).

</div>

&nbsp;

Zero vendor lock-in &mdash; and *we prove it*. Your content lives in clean Markdown and standard Version Control workflows. No proprietary formats. No migration nightmares.

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Want transparency? See for yourself:</span>

Our entire build-system logic for this very website: fewer than 100 lines of code, complete with sophisticated, memoized dependency management that auto-generates multilingual sitemaps, directory indexes, and more.

View the source: [our private source lib tree](https://vcs.sunstarsys.com/repos/svn/public/cms-sites/www.sunstarsys.com/trunk/lib/), or its public [<i class="fa fa-github fa-emoji" title="Github"></i> GitHub mirror](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www/tree/trunk/lib).

The underlying Static Site Generator: open-sourced on GitHub under Apache License 2.0 → @SunStarSys/orion

This isn't marketing spin &mdash; it's verifiable, open engineering heritage dating back to F/OSS innovations pioneered in 2011. Ready to experience a wiki that actually saves time, money, and headaches? [Give us a call or drop us a note](/contact) today.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

<center>
<div class="card border-primary-emphasis fade" style="max-width:25rem;background-color:white;color:#392806">
<div class="card-header">Getting Started</div>
<div class="card-body">

The quickest way to get going is to play with @SunStarSys/orion's default build of <https://iconoclasts.blog> and hollow out the markdown sources in `trunk/content`.  ~90% of the styling customizations are in [`trunk/content/css/local.css`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/content/css/local.css) &mdash; adjust to taste!

The other 10% involves choosing an appropriate bootstrap 5 CSS theme to replace the corresponding files in `content/css/bootstrap.*`; we recommend <https://bootswatch.com> for ideas.

The final step is to rejigger the topmatter navigation menus in `templates/main.html.*`.  Our AI translator will keep everything in sync on demand.

Need help customizing the `Perl` build system in `lib/` and other Django templates in `templates/` to fit your use case?  We are at your service!

</div>
</div>
</center>
</div>
<div class="col-lg-6 border-start" style="border-color: #A9BDBD">

[<img src="index.page/ad-top" style="width: 100%;margin-top: 4px">](features)

&nbsp;

### Here's&nbsp;Why,&nbsp;Young&nbsp;Academic&nbsp;:fa-orcid: / Full&nbsp;Stack&nbsp;Developer&nbsp;:fa-stack-overflow: / Public&nbsp;Blogger&nbsp;:fa-blog:&nbsp;...

&nbsp;

Want a website that's **secure-by-default**? Easy to update and manage, while hiding the complexity of an underlying version control system, yet giving you its full power when you truly need it?  Instant publication when you want it; smooth, staged branch builds and customizable granular promotions to your production site as it suits your team's preferred workflow.

&nbsp;

If you are tired of the per-seat licensing and per-CPU-cycle choices weighing you down whenever you need to fix a typo, [reach out to us](/contact). If you are in charge of content curation and are pining for a customizable facts database to manage your external links, or if you are a regex-equipped lion tamer for decades of accumulated legacy HTML content, or just someone dissatisfied with the other options on the market and how they function at scale, we have something really special to offer you.

&nbsp;

Never having to deal directly with a version control system, or even a static site generator, on your own personal computer is up to you. The online IDE is designed and ready for your **browser-only workflow** whenever you are.  In a pinch, even the mobile (browser) interface will get it done, *instantly*.

<div id="lightning">

![Lightning](index.page/lightning)

</div>

<style type="text/css">

div#lightning img {width:100%}

</style>

&nbsp;

Multi-gigabyte source trees are simply no match for it &mdash; full site build durations are measured in *seconds*, not hours and minutes.  The system easily sustains over [`300 MB/s`](features) while processing your sources for full site builds, but given its <span class="text-white">unique, patent-pending dependency management</span> functionality, it almost never needs to resort to them:

&nbsp;

<center>
<span class="text-primary-emphasis"><i class="fa fa-trowel-bricks"></i> <em>We only build what you need built.</em></span>&trade;
</center>

&nbsp;

Taking architectural cues from [David Wheeler's](https://justatheory.com) famous [Bricolage CMS](https://bricolagecms.org/), this [technology](https://iconoclasts.blog/joe/apache-cms) was first invented in late 2010 by [Paul Querna](https://paul.querna.org/articles/2010/10/22/evolution-of-apaches-websites/), Daniel Shahaf, Dave Fisher, and [Joe Schaefer](https://iconoclasts.blog/joe/) as members of the Apache Infrastructure Team. The phrase "JAMstack" was coined years later (2015), by a group unaware of our prior art in this space.  But the [public record](http://web.archive.org/web/20120112045033/http://www.apache.org/dev/cms) is crystal clear, and this new offering by SunStar Systems is testimony to that original legacy and its true open source origins.

&nbsp;

When Apache software project communities were presented with a free choice between using Confluence-backed sites, or using Orion's roots as the Apache CMS, they overwhelmingly chose the Apache CMS. We think you will too, with its vastly improved Orion!

&nbsp;

<h4>Want to give it a quick spin to see how fast and easy it is?</h4>

This website is self-hosted on Orion; all those hot-pink pencil squares [<i class='fa fa-file-pen text-danger'></i>](https://cms.sunstarsys.com/redirect?uri=https://www.sunstarsys.com/index) at the top right are live.  Feel free to poke around and experiment with anything you see!  The only thing you can't do is commit and watch your changes build and deploy; that's restricted to our personnel for obvious reasons.

Our global Point of Presence (POP) network ensures low-latency connections to both Orion &trade; and the end-delivery websites we host.  We are currently on four continents and have a bicoastal presence within the US.  And we're expanding rapidly- next up Africa and East Asia!

&nbsp;

<h3>It's time for a sea change in how you manage and deliver your site to your target audience.</h3>

&nbsp;

Go at your own pace, use as many employees / previews / edits / commits / branches as you like, and only pay for what you *actually use* on our infrastructure. Just bring your own AI enhanced css/javascript framework, perl scripts, and Django Templates, and we will take care of the rest of your setup at no additional charge. We recommend **Bootstrap 5** for css/js styling, as it is what we use internally; but that is entirely up to you.

In addition, all clients have free, template-customizable or javascript-enabled interfaces to our powerful, proprietary PCRE search engine.

